1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,940
Episode 1: Comrades and Comrades

2
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,720
A date now?

3
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,240
That's right, with Nana-chan.

4
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,820
Don't use other people's
workplace as a meeting spot!

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:14,500
Work

6
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:19,020
This is, you know,
just taking a little break.

7
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,380
Sorry I'm late.

8
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,220
I just got here myself.

9
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:27,820
You've been waiting for an hour already!

10
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,140
Anyway, what about the manuscript?

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,500
I handed it over to the editor.

12
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,100
Hello, everyone.

13
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:34,380
Hello.

14
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,220
That must be tough.

15
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:39,300
Balancing being a Shiraume
officer and a manga artist -

16
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,720
Yeah, it really is.

17
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:43,360
Nana-chan is incredibly busy.

18
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:44,220
Right?

19
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:45,820
W-what, no way.

20
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:49,240
But she's never missed
a single deadline so far.

21
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,280
How admirable.

22
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:54,180
Manga artists are mostly the type who don't keep their deadlines,
you know.

23
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:57,840
Speaking of which, senpai,
are you still running a manga serial?

24
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:58,960
Of course.

25
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,460
I'm the flagship artist for Sapphire! So if Nana-chan has deadlines,
then Ryo-chan too... Well, we've gotten a few calls here.

26
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:14,880
I've never gotten one. Koi-hon, really...
"Yes, that's it, from now on - "

27
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:17,280
Goo.

28
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:23,020
It's Ikemoto!

29
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:25,000
Later, you bastards.

30
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:27,140
Mr. Honda.

31
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:35,200
When you watch TV, turn on the lights
and sit back from the screen, okay?

32
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:48,340
Anyone short on cash, come see me.

33
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:53,060
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

34
00:01:53,060 --> 00:02:00,380
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

35
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:06,800
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

36
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:12,020
You get it, right? Yeah, I get it, I get it.

37
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:15,980
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

38
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,420
Super Editor.

39
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:44,840
No way, Honda!

40
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:06,020
That Helimac!

41
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,300
My bike

42
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,540
My bike

43
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:20,300
Bike

44
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,800
Ryo-san, what do you mean by this?

45
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,640
I should be asking you what you mean.

46
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,180
You, taking advantage of the chaos,

47
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:29,220
were trying to cancel my serialization,
weren't you?

48
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,340
What are you talking about?

49
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:33,840
You didn't tell me today was the deadline,
did you?

50
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:37,160
You don't need to be the fastest, do you?

51
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:39,580
Speed with the pen is the best in the industry,
after all.

52
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,340
Please believe me.

53
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:44,460
Sensei,

54
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,020
well, fine.

55
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,620
Do you have anything to write with?

56
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,960
You're not seriously going to draw here,
are you?

57
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,060
It's fine, even if it's a little shaky.

58
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,480
You've got some right there, don't you?

59
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:57,200
No, not that one.

60
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,500
It's a rookie's manuscript?

61
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,380
Come to think of it,

62
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,560
when a serial artist misses a deadline,

63
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,300
sometimes a rookie's manga ends
up printed in their place, right?

64
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,380
That's a misunderstanding.

65
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:11,340
I'm holding onto this.

66
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,400
No! Give it back!

67
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:14,720
"Holding onto it"?!

68
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:15,960
No!

69
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,340
I said no!

70
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:22,420
Let's make some money! Come on!

71
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:22,900
No way!

72
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:23,660
Well, aren't you something!

73
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:25,140
Please give it back!

74
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:26,340
Stop it, stop...

75
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:30,600
My debut work, of all things!

76
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:31,900
Just as I thought.

77
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:36,040
And one done!

78
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,640
There, it's done.

79
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,000
Good work.

80
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:42,800
I've never seen a manuscript
written on the back of copy paper.

81
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,100
By the way, where are we headed?

82
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,320
To Midori-sensei's apartment.

83
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,380
Midori-sensei.

84
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:52,920
The Midori-sensei who draws
the four-panel gag manga?

85
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,460
Yes.

86
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:58,320
Getting to meet the real Midori-sensei,
I'm so lucky, so lucky!

87
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,060
Midori

88
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,500
I've been waiting, Ryuseijin.

89
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:15,180
Midori, how's the manuscript coming along?

90
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,600
I've already finished it perfectly.

91
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:19,800
You two look just like a couple.

92
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,800
Lucky, lucky.

93
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,000
Awesome. It's so funny my stomach hurts.

94
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,960
Whew, another great one this time.
Good work.

95
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,680
Thank goodness.

96
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:36,140
How about some wine to celebrate
finishing the manuscript?

97
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,200
Wow, that looks delicious.

98
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:41,760
Sorry, but I still have
another place to stop by.

99
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,100
Food and wine!

100
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,980
This is a masterpiece.

101
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:50,360
Natsuki Mimi-sensei, thank you so much.

102
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:55,260
If you go and give me priority again,
you know I'll be happy.

103
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:58,720
I mean it, it's a masterpiece
that will go down in history.

104
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,800
Then shall we pick up some
one-cup sake as a souvenir?

105
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:05,840
Look, I got this car ready just for you.

106
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:09,300
I-I'd love to,
but I still have somewhere to stop by...

107
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:13,200
You're such a charmer.
Next time, you have to keep me company.

108
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,195
Sure,

109
00:06:15,245 --> 00:06:18,920
It's really good!
Go ahead and ink it right away!

110
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:21,460
Wow, Urara is so happy!

111
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,980
Hey, Urara's the only one getting special treatment!
That's not fair!

112
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:26,540
Ryusei-san belongs to everyone!

113
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:27,820
Hey!

114
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,900
Hey, hey,
hurry up and do the inking, will you!

115
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,460
Coming!

116
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:38,200
Senpai, do you think I can head
out for my date with Nana-chan soon?

117
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,300
What? Is what you just said really true?

118
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,000
Yes.

119
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:47,600
If the date gets cancelled,
it could affect the next manuscript.

120
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:50,140
Honda-san, please go on your date right now.

121
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:50,620
Yes.

122
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:54,520
So I'm sending him off right now, Miko.

123
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,640
Yeah, see you later.

124
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,380
Thank you, Ryu Senshi-san.

125
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,400
You really put us manga artists first,
don't you?

126
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:10,020
Being an editor's not a bad racket

127
00:07:10,020 --> 00:07:13,120
Surrounded by beauties like that,
it's like a harem!

128
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:15,100
Let me have a go too, will you?

129
00:07:15,100 --> 00:07:16,080
No way.

130
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:19,380
An editor has to build a
relationship of trust with the artist.

131
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,820
There's really no way?

132
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:22,060
There's really no way.

133
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:23,700
Absolutely, positively not?

134
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:25,060
Absolutely, positively not.

135
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:27,120
Not even if I beg this much?

136
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,200
No matter how much you beg, it's a no.

137
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:37,920
Yeah, it's been a long time Chakabon.

138
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:43,940
We're short on editors, things have changed.
There are two super editors now.

139
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:50,060
Of course it's OK!
You were counting on me, right? Me!

140
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,380
I didn't do it, so there!

141
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,320
So this is Ofrance Publishing

142
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,640
It has the feel of a place
that's about to go under.

143
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,100
I've heard all about you from Ryu.

144
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,380
We're really short-staffed, you see.

145
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,360
We were so desperate,
we'd take anyone, even a cat's paw.

146
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:18,320
Our main title right now
is a men's magazine for men.

147
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,820
It's a weekly,
"Anything Goes Entertainment."

148
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:22,260
Doesn't sound much like a harem, does it.

149
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,200
Well, isn't there anything with
young girls or something like that?

150
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,560
Sure there is.

151
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:32,660
Actually, we're soon publishing
a photo book of Nagisa Shiratori.

152
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:38,360
Nagisa Shiratori, the super-popular
idol who's always on TV lately?

153
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:39,420
Yeah.

154
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:44,780
If this photo book hits big, Office Lice Publishing
will join the ranks of the top publishers.

155
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:47,820
Alright!
Put me in charge of that photo book!

156
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,040
When's the shoot?

157
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:54,360
This is that positive film.

158
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:57,660
That's a nice photo of the child.

159
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:03,480
If we put it up on an internet auction,
it might sell for a good price.

160
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,040
There's a UFO outside the window!

161
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:07,540
Where?

162
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,580
Never mind, I must have been mistaken.

163
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:13,100
Well, I'm counting on you with the work.

164
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:14,100
Yes.

165
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,680
Good morning.

166
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:16,120
I'm home.

167
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:17,560
Deliver the materials.

168
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:18,360
Wait up!

169
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,980
Send this by fax.

170
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:23,420
I'm back! Hurry up!

171
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:23,980
Coming!

172
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,260
Hey, part-timer!

173
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:25,640
Yes!

174
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:33,640
Excuse me,
it's already 11 p.m. at night, you know.

175
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:34,880
So what?

176
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:40,220
Yeah, yeah.

177
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:41,480
Whoa, no, no, not good, not good.

178
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:51,880
Alright, I'm going to really jack
up the part-time pay for this!

179
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:53,780
Fire!

180
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,260
Whoa, the smoke!

181
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:56,080
This is bad!

182
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:57,080
Put it out, quick!

183
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,440
The fire's out.

184
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,540
Thanks for saving us, Ryo-san.

185
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,020
Good work, Baito Cream.

186
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,220
Are you okay? Is anyone hurt?

187
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,540
Still, good thing it
didn't turn into a big fire.

188
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,980
The manuscript for Weekly Nandemo Goraku

189
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:16,280
What?

190
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:20,140
It was supposed to go to the
printer first thing tomorrow morning.

191
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:22,520
At this rate, we won't be able
to get this week's issue out.

192
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:25,500
At this rate,
Off-France Publishing will go under.

193
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,500
It's over.

194
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,200
Wait a minute!

195
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:36,740
I'll take care of this manuscript myself.

196
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:45,100
It's the lead manga in the entertainment
section of the weekly Nandemo magazine.

197
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,540
It's the manuscript from the
funniest manga artist around.

198
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:51,240
And eight whole pages got completely burned.

199
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:54,480
If the sensei's manga isn't in there,
readers won't buy it.

200
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,020
Don't worry, there's nothing to fret about.

201
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,360
Really?

202
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:03,560
There aren't any pages after this, right?

203
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:04,000
Yeah.

204
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,860
Then first, this manuscript...

205
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:09,960
W-what are you doing?

206
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,220
Shut up and watch.

207
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:12,160
Right.

208
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:16,520
Like this, we take one page's
five panels and separate them,

209
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,400
and the first two panels...

210
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:23,420
This is

211
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:26,640
one page is already done.

212
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,620
Next, the car shot.

213
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,020
Flip and enlarge.

214
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:33,800
Yes.

215
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,840
Two pages complete.

216
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:39,220
The still scene is two pages spread across.

217
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,740
Only one page?

218
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:43,280
This is an amazing technique!

219
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:46,720
But we still have five pages left to do.

220
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:49,320
And we've only got this
one panel left, right?

221
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:50,200
What are we going to do?

222
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:52,900
We're going to turn this into five pages?

223
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:55,560
We'll enlarge it little
by little with copies,

224
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:59,020
making it look like it's gradually
coming toward us from the distance.

225
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:04,160
Two pages first, then one page of the character advancing,
then a close-up of the face for one more page.

226
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,000
And the last one continues
with a close-up of the eyes.

227
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,120
What a powerful ending!

228
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:17,280
So, everyone, the 16-page manga is complete!

229
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:21,500
Amazing! We did it!

230
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,800
That's incredible!

231
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,920
It's truly a godsend.

232
00:12:26,820 --> 00:12:28,900
Just as I expected, thank you so much.

233
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,980
This will save our company.

234
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:33,320
This is terrible!

235
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:36,460
Of course,
Midori-sensei's manga got burned too.

236
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:40,560
There's nothing we can do about that one,
is there?

237
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,160
Only two panels survived.

238
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:44,540
Two panels?

239
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:48,280
Of course, Sensei's work too,
if by chance it's lined up alongside

240
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,880
It's Nandemo's flagship series, after all.

241
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:52,580
It's hopeless.

242
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,680
Is this the end of our publishing house?

243
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:58,240
No, we might be able to make it work.

244
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,840
But with only two panels...

245
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,555
Where there's a will, there's a way.

246
00:13:04,605 --> 00:13:07,400
Luckily, it's a dialogue scene.

247
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:18,480
Done!

248
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,580
It's true!

249
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:25,200
So that's how it is. I see.

250
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,820
Say that again. So that's how it is.

251
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:30,060
So that's how it is.

252
00:13:30,060 --> 00:13:33,300
Sorry, it's really hard to hear you.

253
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,260
Once more.

254
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:37,440
Whoa! We're actually having
a proper conversation!

255
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:40,820
Next, it's a blackout.

256
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,900
A blackout? So that's how it is.

257
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:45,660
I see. Yes.

258
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:48,280
A blackout! This is bad.

259
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,340
It's back on. Thank goodness.

260
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,720
Well then it went off again.

261
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,640
Damn, this is bad.

262
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,460
It's back on. Thank goodness.

263
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,380
Oh no, this is bad.

264
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:03,020
Amazing, it's too amazing.

265
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:06,560
If we alternate this
"once more" with the power outages,

266
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:08,340
we can keep going forever.

267
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,640
That's a wonderful technique!

268
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,560
Ruosu-san, could you do this one too?

269
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,040
This one too, this one too, and this one.

270
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:18,500
Leave it to me.

271
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:21,120
I'll make this talk nothing but laughs.

272
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:23,200
Make the numbers bigger here.

273
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,100
Invert this circle.

274
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,440
Enlarge this.

275
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,820
He really is a reliable guy.

276
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,260
Well then,
I'm off to pick up the manuscript.

277
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,160
It's done.

278
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,520
Now we can somehow get it on sale.

279
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,500
You'd better give me a good bonus for this.

280
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,360
Of course.

281
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,540
I have a new respect for you.

282
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,660
Sorry for having you do all the grunt work.

283
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:51,320
From now on, call me Super Editor Ryotsu.

284
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:53,560
Yes, Super Editor Ryotsu-sama.

285
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,440
Shall I bring you some coffee or something?

286
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,240
Japanese tea, please.

287
00:14:57,820 --> 00:15:01,680
This is bad!
The film for Nagisa Shiratori's photobook!

288
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:06,600
W-what is this!
It's almost completely burned!

289
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:10,760
It was supposed to go to the
printer first thing tomorrow morning!

290
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:13,020
At this rate,
we can't release the photobook.

291
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,180
Oh no! It's over!

292
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,420
It's too early to give up!

293
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:23,820
But only five usable panels are left!

294
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,420
Don't worry.

295
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,360
Take this cut, for example.

296
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:38,140
Enlarge it.

297
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,660
Flip it.

298
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:47,100
Lay out the text.

299
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,980
It'll look like a
completely different photo.

300
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,540
Or combine it with another photo.

301
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:07,820
Composite

302
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:13,920
It's realistic.

303
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:18,560
One photo becomes several.

304
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:20,980
As expected of a super editor.

305
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,960
This'll fill up a whole
photobook in no time.

306
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:28,260
But not a single swimsuit
photo that matters is left.

307
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,160
That's right,
it won't sell without swimsuit shots!

308
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:33,320
Swimsuit

309
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:38,580
Now that I think of it, didn't last week's
magazine have Nagisa Shiratori's swimsuit photos

310
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:40,300
That's it.

311
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,740
That's perfect!

312
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:44,360
I'll take these.

313
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,960
They're special photos,
so that's going to be a problem.

314
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,800
I know.

315
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,560
We're in trouble if this goes on.

316
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,840
Change the pose.

317
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:07,660
Add some accessories to change it up.

318
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,880
And change the color of the swimsuit too.

319
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,520
If we go this far, no one will ever notice.

320
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:23,740
Isn't there anything else?

321
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:26,560
This one's nice, but it's black and white.

322
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:27,580
Leave it to me.

323
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:33,020
With a computer, this is a piece of cake.

324
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:44,140
Alright, everyone, find photos we can use.

325
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:55,440
We're short on Hawaii backgrounds,
so let's say she toured the whole world.

326
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,120
Don't we have any other photos?

327
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,260
This is all of them.

328
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:04,700
We're still short 20 pages' worth.

329
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:06,580
Doing all of it with
composites will be tough.

330
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:11,100
I have a few snapshots I took during
the Hawaii location shoot, though.

331
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:13,960
Excellent! Bring them here right away.

332
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,320
Nagisa-chan isn't in many of them, though.

333
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,660
These are all managers and staff.

334
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:20,040
So they won't work after all?

335
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:22,700
No, let's go with this.

336
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:25,440
Just scribble something
in round girly handwriting.

337
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,520
We'll pretend it's her own album.

338
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:28,940
I see.

339
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,960
There are 16 pages left.

340
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:32,760
Make it look like her handwriting.

341
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:36,060
Idol photobooks often have
that kind of writing, right?

342
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:43,060
Getting it from her directly is hard, you know.
Something like that, I'll

343
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:46,520
I'll just dash it off for you.
"The blue sky is lovely."

344
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:53,160
"The white clouds are lovely. Favorite food: steak at a yakiniku place,
confirmed." Nagisa!

345
00:18:54,740 --> 00:19:00,860
Is this really okay? It's an emergency, so, well...
pages. Alright, it's fan service!

346
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:05,580
Nagisa Shiratori, life-size,
an umbrella in hand.

347
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,340
The last page is a footprint.

348
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:11,620
It's like the footprint of a yeti.

349
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:13,280
That's not the image of
Nagisa Shiratori at all.

350
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,520
Good morning.

351
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,120
Good morning, sir.

352
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:19,460
Chocobon, could you come here for a moment?

353
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:20,360
Y-yes?

354
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,560
What is it, President?

355
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,220
How's the progress on the photobook?

356
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,480
Yes, it's going steadily.

357
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,740
That's good to hear.

358
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:34,040
Actually, I was thinking we could double the pages
of that photobook and make it a deluxe edition.

359
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:44,080
This is the president of the production
company Nagisa-chan belongs to.

360
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,380
The president insisted on it, you see.

361
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:50,600
Please make Nagisa's wonderful photobook.

362
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:54,860
But finishing it by tonight is a bit...

363
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,960
I'll pay for it.

364
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:59,920
We took plenty of photos,
so it should be fine.

365
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,100
But...

366
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,220
Leave it to us, Mr. President.

367
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:04,080
And you?

368
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:09,340
I was specially hired to create
Nagisa Shiratori's photobook.

369
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:12,160
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, super editor.

370
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:15,120
I see. That's reassuring.

371
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:15,960
Count on you.

372
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,600
Leave it to us.

373
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,760
In exchange, Mr. President...

374
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:24,940
could you give us a special bonus
based on the photobook's sales?

375
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,040
Sure, sure.

376
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:29,020
Sure, that's the spirit!
You're so generous, Mr. President!

377
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:32,100
It'll be a deluxe 100-page book.

378
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,840
I'm looking forward to it.
Really looking forward to it.

379
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,700
What were you thinking,
agreeing to that so carelessly!

380
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:40,200
There aren't any photos left anyway!

381
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:44,700
Leave it to me! Everyone, bring as
many photos of yourselves as you can!

382
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:47,980
You can actually use this stuff?

383
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,460
Trust my skills!

384
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,547
Nobody will recognize their
elementary school faces anyway,

385
00:20:53,597 --> 00:20:55,500
so we'll say Nagisa is among these.

386
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,760
All the old photos will be her family.

387
00:20:58,900 --> 00:20:59,740
That's awful!

388
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:02,120
Lend me the company brochure!

389
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,120
What are you going to do?

390
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:07,440
We'll put the president's words
on the first page of the photobook.

391
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,100
It'll look just like a graduation album.

392
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:13,740
We'll use Kanto Color for the company
introduction and add a recruitment ad.

393
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:16,580
And the president's profile
and family introduction.

394
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:18,480
That'll fill 20 pages.

395
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:19,320
No way...

396
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:24,840
Then we'll run the novel
Jirochō Gaiden across 30 pages.

397
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:27,900
It's drifting further and
further from an idol photobook.

398
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:29,500
Are we really allowed to put this out?

399
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:30,860
If nobody's going to buy it...

400
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:34,400
It's fine!
Idol photobooks sell no matter what!

401
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:37,420
No matter what's inside,
the fans will buy it!

402
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:38,480
Whoa...

403
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,880
Alright!
The content's all come together for now!

404
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:43,380
Everyone! We have to finish this by tonight!

405
00:21:43,380 --> 00:21:44,300
Aaaaahhh

406
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:50,180
Auntie, the rest is for the president's
daughter and younger sister, and...

407
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:57,180
Enlarging and flipping the eighth one is tough, this round panel is...
As for the photos, though, here...

408
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:04,100
I'm starving.

409
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,860
We have some cup noodles, if that's okay.

410
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,500
I'll take some.

411
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:09,840
Alright.

412
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:12,340
We're finished!

413
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:14,000
We did it!

414
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:16,500
Ryo-san.

415
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:17,880
You really saved us.

416
00:22:28,830 --> 00:22:33,060
Don't you smell something weird?
Yeah, I guess so.

417
00:22:33,910 --> 00:22:35,520
Whaaaat?

418
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:42,400
Aaaaaah!

419
00:22:45,010 --> 00:22:48,160
The blue film's burned! It's all over.

420
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:51,580
Why?

421
00:22:51,580 --> 00:23:00,240
This is ah...
this is Nagisa's positive film.

422
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:06,360
Ryo-san, what on earth is going on here?

423
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:12,720
Well, that's that... I wonder why it
ended up in my pocket. How strange.

424
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,860
Ryo-san

425
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:20,820
Well then,

426
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:26,800
I'll publish a photobook no matter what!

427
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:33,720
This is the Nagisa Shiratori photobook from
Offranche Publishing that's a huge hit right now.

428
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:37,380
It's one photo cut into 400
pieces and made into a book.

429
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:43,060
Fans buy at least three copies: one to look at,
one to assemble, and one to keep safe.

430
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,240
That something like this became a hit...

431
00:23:45,660 --> 00:23:47,320
You never know what's going to sell, do you?

432
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:51,900
I heard this book was inspired by the
change in perspective Ryo-san taught us.

433
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:54,820
Wow, that's amazing, Ryo-chan!

434
00:23:56,960 --> 00:24:00,000
Everyone's happy,
saying they're getting a special bonus!

435
00:24:00,620 --> 00:24:02,020
I should have run away.

436
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:29,640
Was it back then?

437
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:33,720
A mysterious feeling

438
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:39,620
So the tiles of the arcade street

439
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,400
I tried walking only on the black ones

440
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

441
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:57,700
Politicians with their self-important faces

442
00:24:57,700 --> 00:25:01,040
And the aunties with blue eyeshadow too

443
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:06,600
Try turning at that corner

444
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:11,820
You can meet everyone, everyone

445
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:19,760
There's a wall over there,
well, surely there's a wall

446
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:24,940
Everybody come on over to our town!

447
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:26,520
Thank you.

448
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:26,640
Thank you.

449
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:33,700
Yeah, a 20 billion yen
inheritance is coming my way!

450
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:37,460
But if I don't spend half of it within a week,
the rest gets confiscated.

451
00:25:37,900 --> 00:25:41,160
Hey, when it comes to spending money,
this is Ryotsu Kankichi!

452
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:43,720
I won't lose to anyone, anywhere!

453
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:47,000
Next time: Ryo-san becomes a billionaire!

454
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:47,980
See you then!

455
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:59,280
Come on over to our town!

456
00:26:00,260 --> 00:26:00,880
Thank you.

